{"id":466,"date":"2020-10-27T12:55:09","date_gmt":"2020-10-27T19:55:09","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=466"},"modified":"2024-08-30T10:07:19","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T17:07:19","slug":"trimming","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/trimming\/","title":{"rendered":"0F: Trimming"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d9158c7\" name=\"6a2213d9158c7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is trimming?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Each drone has a gyro sensor that helps the drone stabilize and center itself during flight. Occasionally, you might see your drone drift one way without any flight commands or an air current. When this happens, it means the gyro sensor is a little off and it will constantly try to find what it thinks is the correct position.<\/p>\n<p>The best way to fix drifting issues is by changing the trim values. You can do this in two ways. First, you can use the trim buttons on the remote control. Each direction has its own trim button, and those can be found around your remote control\u2019s power button. Whenever you press a trim button, the controller will beep. There will be two beeps when the maximum trim setting is reached.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;467&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]You can also trim using Blockly. When you pair your drone and remote to Blockly, you will see options to change the trim values on the bottom left. We suggest trimming this way because you can actually see the values you are changing.<\/p>\n<p>In this lesson we will go over both ways of trimming.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d9159cc\" name=\"6a2213d9159cc\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drifting backwards<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>If CoDrone Mini drifts backward without any flight commands, press the F button to adjust the trim.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;470&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]On Blockly, increase the pitch value using the &#8216;+&#8217; sign.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2337&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d915a27\" name=\"6a2213d915a27\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drifting forward<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>If CoDrone Mini drifts forward without any flight commands, press the B button on the controller to adjust the trim.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;471&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]On Blockly, decrease the pitch value with the &#8216;-&#8216; sign.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2338&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d915a7c\" name=\"6a2213d915a7c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drifting to the right<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div class=\"activity2__rtf\">\n<p>If CoDrone Mini drifts to the right without any flight commands, press the L button on the controller to adjust the trim.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;472&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]On Blockly, decrease the roll value with the &#8216;-&#8216; sign.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2340&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d915ac6\" name=\"6a2213d915ac6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Drifting to the left<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If CoDrone Mini drifts to the left without any flight commands, press the R button on the controller to adjust the trim.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;473&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]On Blockly, increase the roll value with the &#8216;+&#8217; sign.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;2339&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213d915b0c\" name=\"6a2213d915b0c\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Reset button<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\u2019s possible that CoDrone Mini still won\u2019t be stabilized after trimming. In this case, <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">you can reset the drone sensor by pressing and holding the reset button.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;474&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 7 What is trimming? [vc_column_text]Each drone has a gyro sensor that helps the drone stabilize and center itself during flight. Occasionally, you might see your drone drift one&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/trimming\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1688,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[],"lesson-tag":[2164,2125,2111,2110],"class_list":["post-466","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-remote-control","lesson-tag-trimming","module-getting-started","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/466","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/466\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":8660,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/466\/revisions\/8660"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1688"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=466"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=466"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=466"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}